rcalcemia, but lacks respiratory symptoms to support this in a non-smoker"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Hypercalcemia > 12 mg/dL", "Elevated alkaline phosphatase (suggestive of bone/liver pathology)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "PTH-mediated (parathyroid)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.33898305084745767, "posterior": 0.11104020795907446, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated alkaline phosphatase weakly supports parathyroid-mediated hypercalcemia, but normal serum phosphorus and lack of other features reduce this likelihood."], "evidence_against": ["Normal phosphorus levels weakly argue against PTH-mediated hypercalcemia due to expected hypophosphatemia in primary hyperparathyroidism."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Malignancy-associated (PTHrP / Osteolytic)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.44067796610169496, "posterior": 0.21106286381802553, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The clinical features moderately support malignancy as the cause of hypercalcemia and ALP elevation, though direct evidence (imaging, PTHrP) is lacking."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of direct malignancy evidence (imaging, PTHrP) moderately reduces malignancy likelihood but does not exclude it."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vitamin-D / Granulomatous", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.057, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal phosphorus levels and absence of granulomatous disease findings moderately exclude vitamin D/granulomatous hypercalcemia."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Other (Drug / Endocrine / Immobilization)", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.092, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Sporadic Primary Hyperparathyroidism", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.047, "danger": 0.1, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of described osteopenia reduces the likelihood of sporadic primary hyperparathyroidism (B1.1) and its familial variant (B1.2) due to their characteristic …"]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Familial Primary Hyperparathyroidism (MEN1/2A)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.022, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Negative family history weakly argues against familial hyperparathyroidism (B1.2), maintaining its lower prior probability in the differential."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Parathyroid Carcinoma", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.042, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Solid Tumor with PTHrP Release (e.g., Squamous Cell Carcinoma)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.175, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of tumor imaging or PTHrP confirmation moderately reduces confidence in solid tumor with PTHrP release (B2.1) as the primary explanation."]}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Multiple Myeloma with Osteolytic Lesions", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.031, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": [