umor imaging or PTHrP confirmation moderately reduces confidence in solid tumor with PTHrP release (B2.1) as the primary explanation."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of anemia or Bence Jones proteins in the lab data make multiple myeloma an unlikely explanation for hypercalcemia and ALP elevation?", "summary": "Absence of myeloma-specific lab markers (anemia, Bence Jones proteins) moderately excludes multiple myeloma (B2.2) as the cause of these findings."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of lymphadenopathy or known lymphoma history make cytokine-mediated hypercalcemia (B2.3) less likely than other malignancy-associated causes?", "summary": "Lack of lymphadenopathy and lymphoma history weakly reduces the likelihood of cytokine-mediated hypercalcemia (B2.3), though the presentation remains consistent with lymphoma."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B2", 0.441], ["B1", 0.339], ["B2.1", 0.189]]}, {"top": [["B2", 0.211], ["B2.1", 0.175], ["B1", 0.111]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "Patient is hemodynamically stable with normal vital signs (BP 115/71 mmHg, pulse 72/min, respirations 12/min), no airway compromise, no severe respiratory distress, no acute neurological deficits, and no uncontrolled hemorrhage. Hypercalcemia is subacute (Ca2+ 12.5 mg/dL) without acute end-organ damage.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading hypothesis (B2: malignancy-associated) has posterior 0.44 < 0.75. Dangerous alternatives (B2.1, B2.3) remain unresolved with posterior ≥0.10. Tree depth 2 < max depth 3."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.4, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.17547331991610465, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely explanation of this patient's current presentation?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Antacid overuse"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Increased 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Increased parathyroid hormone"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Malignancy"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Viral illness"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Hyperphosphatemia', 'Abnormality of vitamin D metabolism', 'Abnormality of serum cytokine level', 'Hypercalcemia'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B2", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.441}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B2.1", "label": "Solid Tumor with PTHrP Release (e.g., Squamous Cell Carcinoma)", "posterior": 0.175, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 1, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Lack of tumor imaging or PTHrP confirmation moderately reduces confidence in solid tumor with PTHrP release (B2.1) as t…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B4", "B3"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=60%, source=dxs]\n\nVitamin-D / Granulomatous vs Parathyroid Carcinoma:\n  Favours first:  aching muscles, binge eating, bone pain, depression, digestive problems\n  Favours second: difficulty breathing, difficulty swallowing, frequent loose bowel movements, hoarseness, neck lump\n\nVitamin-D / Granulomatous vs Multiple Myeloma with Osteolytic Lesions:\n  Favours first:  aching muscles, binge eating, depression, digestive problems, dizziness\n  Favours second: anemia, constipation, frequent urination, hypercalcemia, hyperviscosity syndrome\n\nParathyroid Carcinoma vs Multi