parathyroid carcinoma as a diagnosis\n  weight loss → hypercalcemia-induced anorexia and metabolic changes → Solid Tumor with PTHrP Release (e.g., Squamous Cell Carcinoma)\n    (frequency: frequent)\n    Suggestion: Investigate PTH-related protein (PTHrP) levels and perform imaging to identify potential malignancies associated with paraneoplastic hypercalcemia\n  poorly controlled GERD → hypercalcemia-induced gastrointestinal dysfunction → Multiple Myeloma with Osteolytic Lesions\n    (frequency: occasional)\n    Suggestion: Check calcium and albumin levels to assess for hypercalcemia, which could explain both the worsening GERD and systemic symptoms\n\nWhen indirect_reasoning_chains are present, generate candidates that investigate the INTERMEDIATE phenotype to confirm or rule out the indirect association."}
