using hypercalcemia, but lacks respiratory symptoms to support this in a non-smoker"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Hypercalcemia > 12 mg/dL", "Elevated alkaline phosphatase (suggestive of bone/liver pathology)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "PTH-mediated (parathyroid)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0992258534245764, "posterior": 0.08648561250547353, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated alkaline phosphatase weakly supports parathyroid-mediated hypercalcemia, but normal serum phosphorus and lack of other features reduce this likelihood."], "evidence_against": ["Normal phosphorus levels weakly argue against PTH-mediated hypercalcemia due to expected hypophosphatemia in primary hyperparathyroidism."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Malignancy-associated (PTHrP / Osteolytic)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.2743409180069955, "posterior": 0.2117201499485852, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The clinical features moderately support malignancy as the cause of hypercalcemia and ALP elevation, though direct evidence (imaging, PTHrP) is lacking."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of direct malignancy evidence (imaging, PTHrP) moderately reduces malignancy likelihood but does not exclude it."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B